   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "The tests pass with this command, run from the project root (`<run>\\work\\L1\\c\\w`) in Git Bash:\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n```\n\nBoth tests ran and passed (`test_transfer_preserves_total` and `test_rejects_non_positive_amount`).\n\n- **Why `PYTHONPATH=src` is needed:** the package lives in `src/ledgerlite`, and the project has no `pyproject.toml` or `setup.py` to install it. Without that variable, `from ledgerlite import Ledger` fails with an import error. I didn't run it without the variable, so that part is from reading the layout.\n- **Which Python:** I used the `python` on your PATH. The project also has a venv under `.recalith\\runtime\\0.1.0.dev18\\venv`, which I didn't use.\n- **If you use cmd or PowerShell:** the inline `PYTHONPATH=src` syntax won't work there. Set the variable first with `set PYTHONPATH=src` in cmd or `$env:PYTHONPATH=\"src\"` in PowerShell, then run `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.",
