   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "I added `Ledger.close(name)` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`. It raises `ValueError` if the account's balance isn't zero. Otherwise it removes the account. Closing an account that doesn't exist raises `KeyError`, the same as `balance()` does.\n\nI added `test_close_requires_zero_balance` in `tests/test_ledger.py`. It checks that closing fails for both a negative and a positive balance, and that the account is still there afterwards. It then checks that closing succeeds once the balance is back to zero.\n\nThe full suite now runs 3 tests and all pass (`PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`).",
